{"id":"e17t4","name":"API Rate Limiter","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["requests","limit","window"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>An API accepts at most <code>limit</code> requests per client in any window of <code>window</code> seconds. You are given <code>requests</code>, a list of <code>[timestamp, client_id]</code> pairs sorted by timestamp (the timestamp is an integer number of seconds written as a string).</p>\n<p>A request of a client at time <code>t</code> is <b>accepted</b> when the number of <b>accepted</b> requests of the same client with a timestamp in <code>(t - window, t]</code> is strictly less than <code>limit</code>. Refused requests do not count. Each client has its own counter.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return a list of booleans: <code>true</code> when the request at the same position is accepted.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>For <code>requests = [[\"1\", \"a\"], [\"2\", \"a\"], [\"3\", \"a\"], [\"3\", \"b\"], [\"11\", \"a\"], [\"12\", \"a\"]], limit = 2, window = 10</code>, the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">[true, true, false, true, true, true]</pre><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> array.array.string requests<br><b>[input]</b> integer limit<br><b>[input]</b> integer window<br><b>[output]</b> array.boolean</div>","starter":"def solution(requests, limit, window):\n    # write your code here\n    return []\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["fenêtre glissante","deque","dictionnaire de files","requêtes refusées non comptées"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"requests":[["1","a"],["2","a"],["3","a"],["3","b"],["11","a"],["12","a"]],"limit":2,"window":10},"expected":{"value":[true,true,false,true,true,true]}},{"input":{"requests":[["0","x"],["0","x"],["5","x"],["5","x"],["10","x"]],"limit":2,"window":5},"expected":{"value":[true,true,true,true,true]}}],"hidden_n":9,"hidden":"","solution":""}